#import "/commands.typ": *

// woodcore:object heading title
== Purpose of the basis of design
// woodcore:/object title

// woodcore:object text p1
The basis of design translates the service criteria agreement into the technical language of engineers, specialists and contractors. In accordance with SIA 260 (2013), 2.1.3 and 2.5.2, it describes:
// woodcore:/object p1

// woodcore:object text p2
- the hazard scenarios considered;
- the requirements of structural safety, serviceability and durability together with the measures needed to guarantee them, including division of responsibilities, processes, controls and corrective mechanisms;
- the assumed ground conditions;
- the important assumptions in the structural and analytical models;
- the accepted risks;
- other conditions relevant to the design.
// woodcore:/object p2

// woodcore:object text p3
It thus fixes the actions, the material and ground properties, the geometrical properties and the resulting effects. Its extent and content are adapted to the importance of the building, the hazards it is exposed to and the risks it poses to the environment (2.5.3).
// woodcore:/object p3

// woodcore:object text p4
[The requirements of SIA 260 are centred on the structure; this basis of design may extend them to all the building elements concerned (fire protection, building physics, acoustics). It is based on the service criteria agreement of dd.mm.yyyy.]
// woodcore:/object p4
